usage: test_wrapped_scalar_resources.py [-h] --native-build NATIVE_BUILD
                                        --binary BINARY --protocol PROTOCOL
                                        --reference REFERENCE --probe PROBE
                                        --output OUTPUT
                                        [--expected-native-sha256 EXPECTED_NATIVE_SHA256]
                                        --expected-build-sha256 EXPECTED_BUILD_SHA256
                                        [--prepare-only]
                                        [--case {all,entry_guards_and_relative_tokens,saved_scalar_and_temporary_lifetime,result_allocation_oom_recovery}]

Finite wrapped-Scalar64 entry, ownership, and allocation controls. This driver
executes no Torch and derives no floating-point expected values. Its three
recipes are native resource contracts. Only the explicitly selected
positive_one row supplies immutable original numeric bytes. Weak lifetime here
is a native ownership control, not a new Torch compatibility observation.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --native-build NATIVE_BUILD
  --binary BINARY
  --protocol PROTOCOL
  --reference REFERENCE
  --probe PROBE
  --output OUTPUT
  --expected-native-sha256 EXPECTED_NATIVE_SHA256
  --expected-build-sha256 EXPECTED_BUILD_SHA256
  --prepare-only
  --case {all,entry_guards_and_relative_tokens,saved_scalar_and_temporary_lifetime,result_allocation_oom_recovery}
